# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_routes_multidefiner.py" "ROUTES MULTI-DEFINER GATE: PASS" "cross-tier route multi-definer suppression (precision + recall-safe)" "cross-tier ROUTE multi-definer suppression: a route path DEFINED by >1 backend file is AMBIGUOUS (a monorepo's multiple services, or a real app + a copy) -- a single frontend call must NOT false-couple to ALL definers. _cg_routes.match_pairs now counts distinct definers per normalized route and drops a multi-definer route as a coupling anchor, mirroring the sibling P0 guards (openapi #329 / iac #330 / api-contract #332 / config #339, each ~66-91% of their false couples were this class). RECALL-SAFE: single-definer contracts are unaffected; test/fixture-dir files are excluded as DEFINERS (so a real route shadowed by a test app stays single-definer and KEEPS coupling) but KEPT as REQUESTERS (a frontend test that fetches a real route stays coupled). Proven on a crafted repo: multi-real-definer suppressed, single-definer kept, test-shadow real coupling preserved, test-requester coupling preserved, plus a direct match_pairs unit check; content-free path strings only" "cross-tier route coupling no longer false-couples a frontend to every backend that happens to declare the same path -- the multi-definer ambiguity is suppressed exactly like the openapi/iac/api-contract/config sibling detectors, with single-definer recall and test-shadow recall preserved" 16
